NAME
    ingest - read result files, or land.sh's old logs, into the store

SYNOPSIS
    ingest FILE... --runner R --tree SHA [--trial N] [--tier T]
    ingest --backfill [DIR] [--repo DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    A command of the emusen.testing module. Each FILE is a TRX file
    (dotnet test --logger trx) or a JUnit file (nextest's, with its
    flakyFailure and rerunFailure records); its tests become rows under
    their class or crate, in a new trial or the one --trial names. A file
    already read is skipped: its path is the trial's source.

    --backfill reads what land.sh left under DIR (default
    ~/.cache/emusen/tmp): each land/<sha>/ folder as a trial (cargo test's
    per-test lines and counts, dotnet's summary and failed tests, or its
    TRX where one was written, times.txt's wall times, GREEN where a .ok
    file exists); each land-<name>.log transcript, which names the branch
    of the trial its verdict line names or becomes a trial when its folder
    is gone; and the full-suite logs under wiseman-rust/. A folder written
    in the last hour without a .ok file is a land still running and is
    left for the next backfill. Running it again adds only what is new.

    A cargo log is named as land.sh named it, with ' ' and '/' written as
    '_'; it is matched to the crate folders of HEAD, and one no crate
    matches is recorded as cargo:?<name>. See EmuSen_Testing.md §5.

EXAMPLES
    ingest --backfill
    ingest results/wiseman-linux-x64.trx --runner ci --tree 3351e722d
    ingest target/nextest/studio/junit.xml --runner laptop --tree $(git rev-parse HEAD)
